PowerStorm was a "marketing" name applied to many very different cards. 
Some have Linux support, some don't. The ones that come to mind that do 
are the PowerStorm 3D30 (2 MB 8 plane) and 4D20 (16 MB, 24 plane); i.e. 
the TGA2 cards, both thanks to Jay I might add. Also, the PowerStorm 
4D10 which was a Permedia 2 card. The rest do not have any Linux support.

